the conditional's mass, 11.3 eV, free-streams over lambda = 185 Mpc/h (k_nr = 0.0339 h/Mpc)
  for comparison, the structures we observe: clusters at ~1-2 Mpc, galaxies at ~0.03 Mpc, the Lyman-alpha forest
  measures power at k = 1-10 h/Mpc (0.6-6 Mpc), and the galaxy power spectrum at k = 0.05-1 h/Mpc.
  [PASS] A2 THE CONDITIONAL DIES HERE, and it is not close: an 11.3 eV thermal relic free-streams over 190 Mpc, so it erases ALL structure below the supercluster scale -- three orders of magnitude above the clusters it was invoked to explain, and four above the galaxies whose exclusion was its best feature   (lambda_fs = 185 Mpc/h against clusters at 1-2 Mpc and the forest at 0.6-6 Mpc; the relic cannot cluster on the scale of the very objects it must supply)

==================================================================================================================
3. THE ESCAPE, AND WHY THIS FRAMEWORK CANNOT USE IT
==================================================================================================================
  Angus's hot-dark-matter MOND cosmology escapes free-streaming by having MOND GROW structure faster than Newtonian
  gravity does, regrowing the power the relic erased.  That escape is available to MOND cosmologies in general.
  ⚠️ IT IS NOT AVAILABLE TO THIS FRAMEWORK, and the reason is this session's own strongest surviving result:
    the bulk-flow null (hunt_2026/h85_bulk_flow_null.py, the ONE positive that survived a 57-item sweep and its
    three-lens adversarial verification) measured beta = 0.447 against LambdaCDM's f/b = 0.440, where an unprotected
    MOND kernel would require 0.043-0.047 -- a factor of ten away.  The framework's LINEAR regime is NEWTONIAN.
    measured 0.447, LambdaCDM 0.44, unprotected MOND 0.045: the data sit 0.1 sigma from LambdaCDM and 8 sigma from MOND-cosmology growth
  [PASS] A3 THE ESCAPE IS CLOSED BY THE FRAMEWORK'S OWN BEST RESULT: this framework cannot regrow the erased power, because its linear regime was measured to be Newtonian -- and that measurement is the single positive finding that survived the largest sweep of the session.  The conditional is therefore killed by an internal consistency requirement, not by an external datum   (the same result that separates this framework from MOND cosmology (its selling point) forbids it the one escape a hot relic needs)

==================================================================================================================
4. THE RIGOROUS VERSION -- both constraints are the SAME quantity, so the conflict is exact
==================================================================================================================
  MY OWN M2 CAUGHT AN ERROR AND IT MATTERS.  The formula k_nr = 0.018 sqrt(Om) sqrt(m/eV) assumes the species sits at
  the NEUTRINO temperature.  A keV warm-dark-matter particle does not -- it must be produced COLDER or it would
  over-close the universe -- which is why my formula gave 11 Mpc for 3 keV against the published ~0.1 Mpc.  So the
  naive 'm >= 4 keV' bound in the previous version was wrong, and the conditional is NOT dead by a factor of forty.
  Redo it properly.  Hold Omega FIXED at Omega_dm and let production be as cold as it likes:
    number density n ~ T_prod^3 and Omega ~ n m, so at fixed Omega:  T_prod ~ (Omega/m)^(1/3)
    thermal velocity v ~ T_prod/m  =>  v ~ Omega^(1/3) m^(-4/3)  =>  lambda_fs ~ m^(-4/3) at fixed Omega
    meanwhile the Tremaine-Gunn cap is rho_max ~ m^4 sigma^3, which depends on the MASS ALONE and not on production.
  So BOTH constraints are set by m at fixed Omega, and they pull in OPPOSITE directions -- the conflict is structural.
  
  calibration: at m = 11.3 eV thermal production gives exactly Omega_dm, so lambda_fs = 185 Mpc/h is exact there.
      m [eV]   lambda_fs [Mpc/h]   k_fs [h/Mpc]   preserves
        11.3              185.49         0.0339   nothing below superclusters
        30.0               50.46         0.1245   nothing below superclusters
        93.0               11.16         0.5629   galaxy P(k) only
       148.0                6.01         1.0458   galaxy P(k) only
       400.0                1.60         3.9370   forest to k = 1
      1000.0                0.47        13.3585   the full forest
  
  to leave the forest intact at k = 1 h/Mpc (6 Mpc) the relic must be heavier than 148 eV;
  at k = 10 h/Mpc (0.6 Mpc), heavier than 833 eV.
  and phase space demands it be LIGHTER than 93 eV, or it can supply the dwarfs and the framework
  loses the automatic galaxy exclusion that is its one impressive feature.
  [PASS] A4 (THE RIGOROUS KILL, and it is TIGHT rather than a factor of forty) the window is empty by a factor of only 1.6, and it is empty for a structural reason: at fixed Omega, free-streaming needs the relic HEAVIER than 148 eV to spare even the coarsest forest scale, while Tremaine-Gunn needs it LIGHTER than 93 eV to stay out of the dwarfs.  Both constraints are set by the same mass and they pull opposite ways   (phase space demands m <= 93 eV; free-streaming demands m >= 148 eV (k = 1 h/Mpc) or 833 eV (k = 10).  No overlap, and the gap is only 1.6x -- close enough that it is a real physical tension rather than an order-of-magnitude dismissal)
  WHY they conflict, stated exactly: a relic is kept OUT of dwarfs by having LOW primordial phase-space density, and
  kept out of the free-streaming problem by having HIGH primordial phase-space density.  It is one quantity, and the
  conditional needs it small and large at once.  That is not a coincidence of two formulas -- it is the same number.

